---
name: gyrokinetic-details
description: Apply gyrokinetic solver conventions when working on gyrokinetic-related source code or input files.
---

# Instructions

* Use when working on the gyrokinetic/ code, or with an input file that uses
  the gyrokinetic solver.

# Gyrokinetics

## MPI decomposition

Gyrokinetic regression tests parallelize along the last configuration-space
dimension. Choose the partition flag by dimensionality:

| Dimensionality | Flag for N partitions |
|---|---|
| 1x2v | `-c N` |
| 2x2v | `-d N` |
| 3x2v | `-e N` |

For example, run the compiled 2x2v sheath regression on four MPI ranks:

```sh
<mpi_install_prefix>/bin/mpirun -np 4 ./build/gyrokinetic/creg/rt_gk_sheath_2x2v_p1 -M -d 4
```

Use the MPI installation matching the build. `-M` enables MPI in the
regression executable; `-d 4` partitions its second configuration dimension.
Add `-s1` for a one-step smoke test.

See [compiling](../compiling/SKILL.md) when a build is needed,
and [testing-and-verification](../testing-and-verification/SKILL.md) for general test
execution and memory checks.
---
name: naming-conventions
description: Apply Gkeyll naming conventions when creating, editing, or reviewing C, CUDA, or Lua files and code elements.
---

# Instructions

* Apply these naming conventions when creating, editing, or reviewing C, CUDA, and Lua code.

# Naming conventions

### Files.

- Public header files have names starting with gkyl_ and ending in .h.
- Private header files have names starting with gkyl_ and ending in _priv.h.
- CUDA files have names ending in _cu.cu. 
- luareg/ folders have Lua input files whose names end with .lua. The Lua
  wrappers are in the apps/ folders and have names ending in _lw.c

### Functions

- Public functions (defined in public header files) should have a name that starts
  with gkyl_.
- Public functions in files in zero/ folders should have a name that starts
  with the name of the file that contains it.
- Private functions (defined in private header files) or static (and not defined
  in private headers) in files in zero/ folders should have a name that starts
  with an abbreviated version of the name of the file that contains it.

### Variables

- Do not use single letter names for variables whose scope spans more than 15 lines.
- Refer to buffer arrays as "buffer" and not as "scratch". 
---
name: software-design
description: Some design practices in Gkeyll code to consider when implementing new modules (apps, updaters) or modifying existing ones.
---

# Instructions

* Load this skill whenever new modules or updaters in zero/ or apps/ folders
  are to be created, or when existing ones will be edited.

## Software design elements

### Module structure

Most modules in zero/ or apps/ consist of 3 public functions:
1. A creation function, typically called gkyl_<module>_new or gkyl_<module>_init.
2. An execution function, often called gkyl_<module>_advance or gkyl_<module>_apply.
3. A deletion function, typically called gkyl_<module>_release.

There may also be some additional auxiliary private or public functions.

### Module best practices

- All dynamic (heap) allocations should happen in the initialization function,
  and freed in the release function, using the appropriate gkyl_ allocation/deallocation functions when possible.
- Don't place logic branching (e.g. if-statements) that depend on a
  time-independent choice or parameter inside the methods called in the time loop of a simulation
  (e.g. _advance). Instead, use function pointers to set the appropriate method during the initialization
  of the module, and call that method inside the time loop.
- Function signatures in header files should contain a brief comment describing
  what the function does, and a description of each argument following existing styles.
- Comments should follow standard English grammar rules, and culminate with a period (.).
- Methods to initialize an updater in zero/ which take all arguments inside a
  single input struct should have a name with the suffix _inew (instead of _new).

  time-independent choice or parameter inside the methods called in the time loop of a simulation (e.g. _advance). Instead, use function pointers to set the appropriate method during the initialization of the module, and call that method inside the time loop.

### Other principles to follow

- Consider extensibility, maintainability, simplicity and how modular design.
- Avoid code duplication whenever possible (e.g. write functions called
  multiple times) and without breaking layering.
- Write shorter code and refactor into a sub-module whenever possible.
---
name: code_style
description: Gkeyll's C/C++/CUDA code style is enforced by clang-format. Use when writing or editing any .c/.h/.cpp/.hpp/.cu/.cuh file, to know how to format it and which files must never be reformatted.
user-invocable: true
---

# Instructions

* Operate relative to the repo root (detect via `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`).

# Code style

The style itself (indentation, brace placement, spacing, etc.) is defined by the
root `.clang-format` file plus one rule in `ci/format.py` (designated-initializer
layout, see below). Don't try to memorize or restate those rules -- just run the
formatter and let it decide:

```
python3 ci/format.py <file>...
```

Do not run bare `clang-format -i`: it packs designated initializers back onto one
line. `ci/format.py` needs clang-format 18.1.8 on PATH (`pip install clang-format==18.1.8`).

A `pre-commit` hook runs this automatically on commit, and CI (`.github/workflows/format-check.yml`)
double-checks on push/PR, so a file that hasn't been run through clang-format will
get reformatted or flagged regardless.

## The rules the config file can't express: never format `ker/` or `core/minus/`

Two kinds of files must never be run through clang-format, and never hand-formatted
to "match" the style either -- leave them exactly as they are:

- Any path matching `*/ker/*` (e.g. `core/ker/`, `gyrokinetic/ker/`) contains
  auto-generated DG kernel code (see `gkeyll_guide`'s note on `ker/`: generated with
  Maxima, never hand-edited).
- Anything under `core/minus/` is a vendored third-party library (e.g. sqlite3,
  kann, pcg_basic, STC), not Gkeyll's own code.

The pre-commit hook and CI already exclude both for this reason.

## Designated initializers: the script decides, not the trailing comma

A designated initializer that fits on one line stays on one line. One that does
not gets one member per line, first member below the `{`, closing `}` on its own
line. `ci/format.py` enforces this by stripping every trailing comma, running
clang-format, re-adding a trailing comma to each list that did not fit, and running
clang-format again. So don't add or remove trailing commas to steer the layout;
write the list any way you like and run the script.

## Two conventions the formatter enforces that you should know when reading code

- Every function *definition* has its return type on its own line, so
  `grep '^gkyl_foo('` finds the definition. Declarations keep the type on the same line.
- `case` labels are indented one level inside `switch`.
#include <assert.h>
#include <math.h>
#include <gkyl_alloc.h>
#include <gkyl_array_ops.h>
#include <gkyl_gk_fluid_moments_priv.h>

// Copy one DG component directly, including between vector arrays.
static void
gk_fluid_moments_copy(
  const struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *up, const struct gkyl_range *range, struct gkyl_array *out,
  int oc, double rmass_fac, const struct gkyl_array *inp, int ic
)
{
  int nb = up->basis.num_basis;
  gkyl_array_set_offset_ncoeff_range(out, rmass_fac, inp, nb, ic * nb, oc * nb, range);
}

static void
gk_fluid_moments_perp(
  const struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *up, const struct gkyl_range *range,
  const struct gkyl_array *state
)
{
  gkyl_dg_mul_op_range(&up->basis, 0, up->pperp, 0, up->bmag, 3, state, range);
}

static void
gk_fluid_moments_perp_zero(
  const struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *up, const struct gkyl_range *range,
  const struct gkyl_array *state
)
{
  gkyl_array_clear_range(up->pperp, 0.0, range);
}

static void
gk_fluid_moments_project_perp(
  const struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *up, const struct gkyl_range *range,
  const struct gkyl_array *state, const struct gkyl_array *prim
)
{
  gkyl_dg_mul_op_range(&up->basis, 0, up->pperp, 0, state, 3, prim, range);
}

static void
gk_fluid_moments_project_perp_zero(
  const struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *up, const struct gkyl_range *range,
  const struct gkyl_array *state, const struct gkyl_array *prim
)
{
  gkyl_array_clear_range(up->pperp, 0.0, range);
}

// Recover u and weighted pressures. No division by J is needed.
static void
gk_fluid_moments_recover(
  const struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *up, const struct gkyl_range *range,
  const struct gkyl_array *state
)
{
  gkyl_dg_div_op_range(up->mem, &up->basis, 0, up->upar, 1, state, 0, state, range);
  up->perp(up, range, state);
  gkyl_dg_mul_op_range(&up->basis, 0, up->ppar, 0, up->upar, 1, state, range);
  gkyl_array_scale_range(up->ppar, -1.0, range);
  gkyl_array_set_offset_range(up->tmp, 2.0, state, 2 * up->basis.num_basis, range);
  gkyl_array_accumulate_range(up->ppar, 1.0, up->tmp, range);
  gkyl_array_accumulate_range(up->ppar, -2.0, up->pperp, range);
}

static void
gk_fluid_moments_linear(
  const struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *up, const struct gkyl_range *range,
  const struct gkyl_array *state, const struct gkyl_array *phi
)
{
  gk_fluid_moments_copy(up, range, up->result, 0, up->rmass_fac, state, up->component);
}

static void
gk_fluid_moments_m2perp(
  const struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *up, const struct gkyl_range *range,
  const struct gkyl_array *state, const struct gkyl_array *phi
)
{
  up->perp(up, range, state);
  gk_fluid_moments_copy(up, range, up->result, 0, 2.0 / up->mass, up->pperp, 0);
}

static void
gk_fluid_moments_m2par(
  const struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *up, const struct gkyl_range *range,
  const struct gkyl_array *state, const struct gkyl_array *phi
)
{
  up->perp(up, range, state);
  gkyl_array_set_offset_range(up->ppar, 2.0 / up->mass, state, 2 * up->basis.num_basis, range);
  gkyl_array_accumulate_range(up->ppar, -2.0 / up->mass, up->pperp, range);
  gk_fluid_moments_copy(up, range, up->result, 0, 1.0, up->ppar, 0);
}

static void
gk_fluid_moments_m3par(
  const struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *up, const struct gkyl_range *range,
  const struct gkyl_array *state, const struct gkyl_array *phi
)
{
  gk_fluid_moments_recover(up, range, state);
  // M3par = u*(M2par+2*J*ppar/m).
  gkyl_array_scale_range(up->ppar, 2.0 / up->mass, range);
  gkyl_array_set_offset_range(up->tmp, 2.0 / up->mass, state, 2 * up->basis.num_basis, range);
  gkyl_array_accumulate_range(up->ppar, 1.0, up->tmp, range);
  gkyl_array_accumulate_range(up->ppar, -2.0 / up->mass, up->pperp, range);
  gkyl_dg_mul_op_range(&up->basis, 0, up->result, 0, up->upar, 0, up->ppar, range);
}

static void
gk_fluid_moments_m3perp(
  const struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *up, const struct gkyl_range *range,
  const struct gkyl_array *state, const struct gkyl_array *phi
)
{
  gkyl_dg_div_op_range(up->mem, &up->basis, 0, up->upar, 1, state, 0, state, range);
  up->perp(up, range, state);
  gkyl_array_scale_range(up->pperp, 2.0 / up->mass, range);
  gkyl_dg_mul_op_range(&up->basis, 0, up->result, 0, up->upar, 0, up->pperp, range);
}

static void
gk_fluid_moments_maxwellian(
  const struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *up, const struct gkyl_range *range,
  const struct gkyl_array *state, const struct gkyl_array *phi
)
{
  gk_fluid_moments_recover(up, range, state);
  gk_fluid_moments_copy(up, range, up->result, 0, 1.0 / up->mass, state, 0);
  gk_fluid_moments_copy(up, range, up->result, 1, 1.0, up->upar, 0);
  gkyl_array_accumulate_range(up->ppar, 2.0, up->pperp, range);
  gkyl_array_scale_range(up->ppar, 1.0 / (2 * up->vdim - 1), range);
  gkyl_dg_div_op_range(up->mem, &up->basis, 2, up->result, 0, up->ppar, 0, state, range);
}

static void
gk_fluid_moments_bimaxwellian(
  const struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *up, const struct gkyl_range *range,
  const struct gkyl_array *state, const struct gkyl_array *phi
)
{
  gk_fluid_moments_recover(up, range, state);
  gk_fluid_moments_copy(up, range, up->result, 0, 1.0 / up->mass, state, 0);
  gk_fluid_moments_copy(up, range, up->result, 1, 1.0, up->upar, 0);
  gkyl_dg_div_op_range(up->mem, &up->basis, 2, up->result, 0, up->ppar, 0, state, range);
  gkyl_dg_div_op_range(up->mem, &up->basis, 3, up->result, 0, up->pperp, 0, state, range);
}

static void
gk_fluid_moments_m0m1m2(
  const struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *up, const struct gkyl_range *range,
  const struct gkyl_array *state, const struct gkyl_array *phi
)
{
  for (int c = 0; c < 3; ++c) {
    gk_fluid_moments_copy(up, range, up->result, c, (c == 2 ? 2.0 : 1.0) / up->mass, state, c);
  }
}

static void
gk_fluid_moments_m0m1m2parperp(
  const struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *up, const struct gkyl_range *range,
  const struct gkyl_array *state, const struct gkyl_array *phi
)
{
  gk_fluid_moments_m0m1m2(up, range, state, phi);
  up->perp(up, range, state);
  gkyl_array_set_offset_range(up->ppar, 2.0 / up->mass, state, 2 * up->basis.num_basis, range);
  gkyl_array_accumulate_range(up->ppar, -2.0 / up->mass, up->pperp, range);
  gk_fluid_moments_copy(up, range, up->result, 2, 1.0, up->ppar, 0);
  gk_fluid_moments_copy(up, range, up->result, 3, 2.0 / up->mass, up->pperp, 0);
}

static void
gk_fluid_moments_hamiltonian(
  const struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *up, const struct gkyl_range *range,
  const struct gkyl_array *state, const struct gkyl_array *phi
)
{
  assert(phi);
  gk_fluid_moments_copy(up, range, up->result, 0, 1.0 / up->mass, state, 0);
  gk_fluid_moments_copy(up, range, up->result, 1, 1.0, state, 1);
  gkyl_dg_mul_op_range(&up->basis, 0, up->ppar, 0, phi, 0, state, range);
  gkyl_array_scale_range(up->ppar, up->charge / up->mass, range);
  gkyl_array_set_offset_range(up->tmp, 1.0, state, 2 * up->basis.num_basis, range);
  gkyl_array_accumulate_range(up->ppar, 1.0, up->tmp, range);
  gk_fluid_moments_copy(up, range, up->result, 2, 1.0, up->ppar, 0);
}

static void
gk_fluid_moments_finish(
  const struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *up, const struct gkyl_range *range, struct gkyl_array *out
)
{
  for (int c = 0; c < up->num_mom; ++c) {
    gk_fluid_moments_copy(up, range, out, c, 1.0, up->result, c);
  }
}

static void
gk_fluid_moments_integrate(
  const struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *up, const struct gkyl_range *range, struct gkyl_array *out
)
{
  struct gkyl_range_iter iter;
  gkyl_range_iter_init(&iter, range);
  while (gkyl_range_iter_next(&iter)) {
    long loc = gkyl_range_idx(range, iter.idx);
    const double *dg = gkyl_array_cfetch(up->result, loc);
    double *integral = gkyl_array_fetch(out, loc);
    for (int c = 0; c < up->num_mom; ++c) {
      integral[c] = up->volnorm_fac * dg[c * up->basis.num_basis];
    }
  }
}

struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *
gkyl_gk_fluid_moments_inew(const struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments_inp *inp)
{
  assert(inp->vdim == 1 || inp->vdim == 2);
  assert(inp->mass > 0 && inp->bmag);

  struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *up = gkyl_malloc(sizeof *up);

  *up = (struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments){
    .basis = *inp->basis,
    .vdim = inp->vdim,
    .mass = inp->mass,
    .charge = inp->charge,
    .num_mom = 1,
    .num_cells = inp->range->volume,
    .rmass_fac = 1.0 / inp->mass,
    .volnorm_fac = 1.0,
    .perp = inp->vdim == 1 ? gk_fluid_moments_perp_zero : gk_fluid_moments_perp,
    .project_perp = inp->vdim == 1 ? gk_fluid_moments_project_perp_zero :
                                     gk_fluid_moments_project_perp,
    .finish = inp->integrated ? gk_fluid_moments_integrate : gk_fluid_moments_finish,
  };

#pragma once

#include <gkyl_array.h>
#include <gkyl_basis.h>
#include <gkyl_mom_type.h>
#include <gkyl_range.h>
#include <gkyl_rect_grid.h>

struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments;

struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments_inp {
  const struct gkyl_basis *basis; // Configuration-space basis.
  const struct gkyl_rect_grid *grid; // Configuration-space grid.
  const struct gkyl_range *range, *range_ext; // Interior and extended ranges.
  const struct gkyl_array *bmag; // Magnetic magnitude (acquired by updater).
  int vdim; // Physical velocity dimension: 1 or 2.
  double mass, charge; // Species mass and charge.
  enum gkyl_distribution_moments moment; // Moment to calculate.
  bool integrated; // Return cell integrals instead of DG coefficients.
  bool use_gpu; // Allocate scratch on the GPU.
};

/**
 * Create weak-DG conversions and Maxwellian closures for J*(rho,Mpar,E,pperp/B).
 *
 * @param inp Configuration and geometry; arrays must reside on the selected device.
 */
struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *gkyl_gk_fluid_moments_inew(const struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments_inp *inp
);

/**
 * Return the number of output moments.
 * @param up Fluid moment updater.
 */
int gkyl_gk_fluid_moments_num_mom(const struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *up);

/**
 * Calculate moments, retaining J on densities but not on primitive u and T/m.
 *
 * @param up Fluid moment updater.
 * @param range Configuration range used at initialization.
 * @param state Conservative state J*(rho,Mpar,E,pperp/B).
 * @param phi Potential, required only for Hamiltonian moments.
 * @param out Output DG moments or cell integrals.
 */
void gkyl_gk_fluid_moments_advance(
  const struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *up, const struct gkyl_range *range,
  const struct gkyl_array *state, const struct gkyl_array *phi, struct gkyl_array *out
);

/**
 * Convert primitive fields using weighted-first weak products.
 *
 * @param up Fluid moment updater.
 * @param range Configuration range used at initialization.
 * @param prim Fields (n,upar,Tpar/m,Tperp/m), without J; Tperp is ignored in 1v.
 * @param jacobgeo Configuration-space Jacobian.
 * @param state Output J*(rho,Mpar,E,pperp/B); must not alias prim.
 */
void gkyl_gk_fluid_moments_from_prim(
  const struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *up, const struct gkyl_range *range,
  const struct gkyl_array *prim, const struct gkyl_array *jacobgeo, struct gkyl_array *state
);

/**
 * Scale all conserved fields by target/current density, then set rho exactly.
 *
 * @param up Fluid moment updater.
 * @param range Configuration range used at initialization.
 * @param density Target J*n, not modified.
 * @param state Conservative state to rescale in place.
 */
void gkyl_gk_fluid_moments_set_density(
  const struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *up, const struct gkyl_range *range,
  const struct gkyl_array *density, struct gkyl_array *state
);

/**
 * Release updater and scratch.
 *
 * @param up Fluid moment updater.
 */
void gkyl_gk_fluid_moments_release(struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *up);

