---
name: software-design
description: Some design practices in Gkeyll code to consider when implementing new modules (apps, updaters) or modifying existing ones.
---

# Instructions

* Load this skill whenever new modules or updaters in zero/ or apps/ folders
  are to be created, or when existing ones will be edited.

## Software design elements

### Module structure

Most modules in zero/ or apps/ consist of 3 public functions:
1. A creation function, typically called gkyl_<module>_new or gkyl_<module>_init.
2. An execution function, often called gkyl_<module>_advance or gkyl_<module>_apply.
3. A deletion function, typically called gkyl_<module>_release.

There may also be some additional auxiliary private or public functions.

### Module best practices

- All dynamic (heap) allocations should happen in the initialization function,
  and freed in the release function, using the appropriate gkyl_ allocation/deallocation functions when possible.
- Don't place logic branching (e.g. if-statements) that depend on a
  time-independent choice or parameter inside the methods called in the time loop of a simulation
  (e.g. _advance). Instead, use function pointers to set the appropriate method during the initialization
  of the module, and call that method inside the time loop.
- Function signatures in header files should contain a brief comment describing
  what the function does, and a description of each argument following existing styles.
- Comments should follow standard English grammar rules, and culminate with a period (.).
- Methods to initialize an updater in zero/ which take all arguments inside a
  single input struct should have a name with the suffix _inew (instead of _new).

  time-independent choice or parameter inside the methods called in the time loop of a simulation (e.g. _advance). Instead, use function pointers to set the appropriate method during the initialization of the module, and call that method inside the time loop.

### Other principles to follow

- Consider extensibility, maintainability, simplicity and how modular design.
- Avoid code duplication whenever possible (e.g. write functions called
  multiple times) and without breaking layering.
- Write shorter code and refactor into a sub-module whenever possible.
---
name: gyrokinetic-details
description: Apply gyrokinetic solver conventions when working on gyrokinetic-related source code or input files.
---

# Instructions

* Use when working on the gyrokinetic/ code, or with an input file that uses
  the gyrokinetic solver.

# Gyrokinetics

## MPI decomposition

Gyrokinetic regression tests parallelize along the last configuration-space
dimension. Choose the partition flag by dimensionality:

| Dimensionality | Flag for N partitions |
|---|---|
| 1x2v | `-c N` |
| 2x2v | `-d N` |
| 3x2v | `-e N` |

For example, run the compiled 2x2v sheath regression on four MPI ranks:

```sh
<mpi_install_prefix>/bin/mpirun -np 4 ./build/gyrokinetic/creg/rt_gk_sheath_2x2v_p1 -M -d 4
```

Use the MPI installation matching the build. `-M` enables MPI in the
regression executable; `-d 4` partitions its second configuration dimension.
Add `-s1` for a one-step smoke test.

See [compiling](../compiling/SKILL.md) when a build is needed,
and [testing-and-verification](../testing-and-verification/SKILL.md) for general test
execution and memory checks.
---
name: naming-conventions
description: Apply Gkeyll naming conventions when creating, editing, or reviewing C, CUDA, or Lua files and code elements.
---

# Instructions

* Apply these naming conventions when creating, editing, or reviewing C, CUDA, and Lua code.

# Naming conventions

### Files.

- Public header files have names starting with gkyl_ and ending in .h.
- Private header files have names starting with gkyl_ and ending in _priv.h.
- CUDA files have names ending in _cu.cu. 
- luareg/ folders have Lua input files whose names end with .lua. The Lua
  wrappers are in the apps/ folders and have names ending in _lw.c

### Functions

- Public functions (defined in public header files) should have a name that starts
  with gkyl_.
- Public functions in files in zero/ folders should have a name that starts
  with the name of the file that contains it.
- Private functions (defined in private header files) or static (and not defined
  in private headers) in files in zero/ folders should have a name that starts
  with an abbreviated version of the name of the file that contains it.

### Variables

- Do not use single letter names for variables whose scope spans more than 15 lines.
- Refer to buffer arrays as "buffer" and not as "scratch". 
#include <assert.h>
#include <math.h>
#include <gkyl_alloc.h>
#include <gkyl_array_ops.h>
#include <gkyl_gk_fluid_moments_priv.h>

// Allocate a double array on the requested device.
static struct gkyl_array *
mkarr(bool use_gpu, long nc, long size)
{
  return use_gpu ? gkyl_array_cu_dev_new(GKYL_DOUBLE, nc, size) :
                   gkyl_array_new(GKYL_DOUBLE, nc, size);
}

// The state is J*(rho,Mpar,E,pperp/B), with Mpar=rho*u and u the parallel velocity.
// Moment densities below include J; primitive u and T/m do not.
// Products and quotients of fields are evaluated with weak-DG operations.

// Get the weighted perpendicular pressure: J*pperp = B*state[3].
static void
gk_fluid_moments_calc_Jpperp_from_state(
  const struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *up, const struct gkyl_range *range,
  const struct gkyl_array *state
)
{
  gkyl_dg_mul_op_range(&up->basis, 0, up->pperp, 0, up->bmag, 3, state, range);
}

// Construct the weighted perpendicular pressure: J*pperp = (J*rho)*(Tperp/m).
static void
gk_fluid_moments_calc_Jpperp_from_prim(
  const struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *up, const struct gkyl_range *range,
  const struct gkyl_array *state, const struct gkyl_array *prim
)
{
  gkyl_dg_mul_op_range(&up->basis, 0, up->pperp, 0, state, 3, prim, range);
}

// Calculate:
//   upar = (J*Mpar)/(J*rho),
//   J*pperp = B*state[3],
//   J*ppar = 2*J*E-upar*(J*Mpar)-2*J*pperp.
static void
gk_fluid_moments_calc_upar_pressures(
  const struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *up, const struct gkyl_range *range,
  const struct gkyl_array *state
)
{
  gkyl_dg_div_op_range(up->mem, &up->basis, 0, up->upar, 1, state, 0, state, range);
  gk_fluid_moments_calc_Jpperp_from_state(up, range, state);
  gkyl_dg_mul_op_range(&up->basis, 0, up->ppar, 0, up->upar, 1, state, range);
  gkyl_array_scale_range(up->ppar, -1.0, range);
  gkyl_array_accumulate_offset_range(up->ppar, 2.0, state, 2 * up->basis.num_basis, range);
  gkyl_array_accumulate_range(up->ppar, -2.0, up->pperp, range);
}

// Compute M0, M1, or M2 by scaling the selected conserved field:
// result = rmass_fac*state[component].
static void
gk_fluid_moments_m0_or_m1_or_m2(
  const struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *up, const struct gkyl_range *range,
  const struct gkyl_array *state, const struct gkyl_array *phi
)
{
  int nb = up->basis.num_basis;
  gkyl_array_set_offset_ncoeff_range(
    up->result, up->rmass_fac, state, nb, up->component * nb, 0, range
  );
}

// Compute the perpendicular second moment: M2perp = 2*J*pperp/m.
static void
gk_fluid_moments_m2perp(
  const struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *up, const struct gkyl_range *range,
  const struct gkyl_array *state, const struct gkyl_array *phi
)
{
  int nb = up->basis.num_basis;
  gk_fluid_moments_calc_Jpperp_from_state(up, range, state);
  gkyl_array_set_offset_ncoeff_range(up->result, 2.0 / up->mass, up->pperp, nb, 0, 0, range);
}

// Compute the parallel second moment: M2par = 2*(J*E-J*pperp)/m.
static void
gk_fluid_moments_m2par(
  const struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *up, const struct gkyl_range *range,
  const struct gkyl_array *state, const struct gkyl_array *phi
)
{
  int nb = up->basis.num_basis;
  gk_fluid_moments_calc_Jpperp_from_state(up, range, state);
  gkyl_array_set_offset_range(up->ppar, 2.0 / up->mass, state, 2 * up->basis.num_basis, range);
  gkyl_array_accumulate_range(up->ppar, -2.0 / up->mass, up->pperp, range);
  gkyl_array_set_offset_ncoeff_range(up->result, 1.0, up->ppar, nb, 0, 0, range);
}

// Close the parallel third moment: M3par = upar*(M2par+2*J*ppar/m).
static void
gk_fluid_moments_m3par(
  const struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *up, const struct gkyl_range *range,
  const struct gkyl_array *state, const struct gkyl_array *phi
)
{
  gk_fluid_moments_calc_upar_pressures(up, range, state);
  gkyl_array_scale_range(up->ppar, 2.0 / up->mass, range);
  gkyl_array_accumulate_offset_range(
    up->ppar, 2.0 / up->mass, state, 2 * up->basis.num_basis, range
  );
  gkyl_array_accumulate_range(up->ppar, -2.0 / up->mass, up->pperp, range);
  gkyl_dg_mul_op_range(&up->basis, 0, up->result, 0, up->upar, 0, up->ppar, range);
}

// Close the perpendicular third moment: M3perp = upar*(2*J*pperp/m).
static void
gk_fluid_moments_m3perp(
  const struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *up, const struct gkyl_range *range,
  const struct gkyl_array *state, const struct gkyl_array *phi
)
{
  gkyl_dg_div_op_range(up->mem, &up->basis, 0, up->upar, 1, state, 0, state, range);
  gk_fluid_moments_calc_Jpperp_from_state(up, range, state);
  gkyl_array_scale_range(up->pperp, 2.0 / up->mass, range);
  gkyl_dg_mul_op_range(&up->basis, 0, up->result, 0, up->upar, 0, up->pperp, range);
}

// Compute:
//   J*n = J*rho/m,
//   upar = (J*Mpar)/(J*rho),
//   T/m = (J*ppar+2*J*pperp)/(3*J*rho).
static void
gk_fluid_moments_maxwellian(
  const struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *up, const struct gkyl_range *range,
  const struct gkyl_array *state, const struct gkyl_array *phi
)
{
  int nb = up->basis.num_basis;
  gk_fluid_moments_calc_upar_pressures(up, range, state);
  gkyl_array_set_offset_ncoeff_range(up->result, 1.0 / up->mass, state, nb, 0, 0, range);
  gkyl_array_set_offset_ncoeff_range(up->result, 1.0, up->upar, nb, 0, nb, range);
  gkyl_array_accumulate_range(up->ppar, 2.0, up->pperp, range);
  gkyl_array_scale_range(up->ppar, 1.0 / 3.0, range);
  gkyl_dg_div_op_range(up->mem, &up->basis, 2, up->result, 0, up->ppar, 0, state, range);
}

// Compute:
//   J*n = J*rho/m,
//   upar = (J*Mpar)/(J*rho),
//   Tpar/m = (J*ppar)/(J*rho),
//   Tperp/m = (J*pperp)/(J*rho).
static void
gk_fluid_moments_bimaxwellian(
  const struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *up, const struct gkyl_range *range,
  const struct gkyl_array *state, const struct gkyl_array *phi
)
{
  int nb = up->basis.num_basis;
  gk_fluid_moments_calc_upar_pressures(up, range, state);
  gkyl_array_set_offset_ncoeff_range(up->result, 1.0 / up->mass, state, nb, 0, 0, range);
  gkyl_array_set_offset_ncoeff_range(up->result, 1.0, up->upar, nb, 0, nb, range);
  gkyl_dg_div_op_range(up->mem, &up->basis, 2, up->result, 0, up->ppar, 0, state, range);
  gkyl_dg_div_op_range(up->mem, &up->basis, 3, up->result, 0, up->pperp, 0, state, range);
}

// Compute the combined moments: (M0,M1,M2) = (J*rho/m,J*Mpar/m,2*J*E/m).
static void
gk_fluid_moments_m0m1m2(
  const struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *up, const struct gkyl_range *range,
  const struct gkyl_array *state, const struct gkyl_array *phi
)
{
  int nb = up->basis.num_basis;
  for (int c = 0; c < 3; ++c) {
    gkyl_array_set_offset_ncoeff_range(
      up->result, (c == 2 ? 2.0 : 1.0) / up->mass, state, nb, c * nb, c * nb, range
    );
  }
}

// Compute (M0,M1,M2par,M2perp) =
// (J*rho/m,J*Mpar/m,2*(J*E-J*pperp)/m,2*J*pperp/m).
static void
gk_fluid_moments_m0m1m2parperp(
  const struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *up, const struct gkyl_range *range,
  const struct gkyl_array *state, const struct gkyl_array *phi
)
{
  int nb = up->basis.num_basis;
  gk_fluid_moments_m0m1m2(up, range, state, phi);
  gk_fluid_moments_calc_Jpperp_from_state(up, range, state);
  gkyl_array_set_offset_range(up->ppar, 2.0 / up->mass, state, 2 * up->basis.num_basis, range);
  gkyl_array_accumulate_range(up->ppar, -2.0 / up->mass, up->pperp, range);
  gkyl_array_set_offset_ncoeff_range(up->result, 1.0, up->ppar, nb, 0, 2 * nb, range);
  gkyl_array_set_offset_ncoeff_range(up->result, 2.0 / up->mass, up->pperp, nb, 0, 3 * nb, range);
}

// Compute density, parallel momentum, and Hamiltonian density:
// (J*n,J*Mpar,J*E+q*phi*(J*n)), with J*n = J*rho/m.
static void
gk_fluid_moments_hamiltonian(
  const struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *up, const struct gkyl_range *range,
  const struct gkyl_array *state, const struct gkyl_array *phi
)
{
  int nb = up->basis.num_basis;
  assert(phi);
  gkyl_array_set_offset_ncoeff_range(up->result, 1.0 / up->mass, state, nb, 0, 0, range);
  gkyl_array_set_offset_ncoeff_range(up->result, 1.0, state, nb, nb, nb, range);
  gkyl_dg_mul_op_range(&up->basis, 0, up->ppar, 0, phi, 0, state, range);
  gkyl_array_scale_range(up->ppar, up->charge / up->mass, range);
  gkyl_array_accumulate_offset_range(up->ppar, 1.0, state, 2 * up->basis.num_basis, range);
  gkyl_array_set_offset_ncoeff_range(up->result, 1.0, up->ppar, nb, 0, 2 * nb, range);
}

// Copy the requested DG moment components from the result buffer to out.
static void
gk_fluid_moments_final_copy(
  const struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *up, const struct gkyl_range *range, struct gkyl_array *out
)
{
  int nb = up->basis.num_basis;
  for (int c = 0; c < up->num_mom; ++c) {
    gkyl_array_set_offset_ncoeff_range(out, 1.0, up->result, nb, c * nb, c * nb, range);
  }
}

// Integrate each moment over a cell: integral[c] = product_d(dx[d]/sqrt(2))*q[c,0],
// where q[c,0] is the constant DG coefficient of moment c.
static void
gk_fluid_moments_integrate(
  const struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *up, const struct gkyl_range *range, struct gkyl_array *out
)
{
  struct gkyl_range_iter iter;
  gkyl_range_iter_init(&iter, range);
  while (gkyl_range_iter_next(&iter)) {
    long loc = gkyl_range_idx(range, iter.idx);
    const double *dg = gkyl_array_cfetch(up->result, loc);
    double *integral = gkyl_array_fetch(out, loc);
    for (int c = 0; c < up->num_mom; ++c) {
      integral[c] = up->volnorm_fac * dg[c * up->basis.num_basis];
    }
  }
}

struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *
gkyl_gk_fluid_moments_inew(const struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments_inp *inp)
{
  assert(inp->mass > 0 && inp->bmag);

  struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *up = gkyl_malloc(sizeof *up);

  *up = (struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments){
    .basis = *inp->basis,
    .mass = inp->mass,
    .charge = inp->charge,
    .num_mom = 1,
    .num_cells = inp->range->volume,
    .rmass_fac = 1.0 / inp->mass,
    .volnorm_fac = 1.0,
    .final_func = inp->integrated ? gk_fluid_moments_integrate : gk_fluid_moments_final_copy,
  };

  switch (inp->moment) {
    case GKYL_F_MOMENT_M0:
    case GKYL_F_MOMENT_M1:
    case GKYL_F_MOMENT_M2:
      up->component = inp->moment == GKYL_F_MOMENT_M0 ? 0 : inp->moment == GKYL_F_MOMENT_M1 ? 1 : 2;
      up->rmass_fac *= inp->moment == GKYL_F_MOMENT_M1 == 2 ? 2.0 : 1.0;
      up->calc_func = gk_fluid_moments_m0_or_m1_or_m2;
      break;
    case GKYL_F_MOMENT_M2PAR:
      up->calc_func = gk_fluid_moments_m2par;
      break;
    case GKYL_F_MOMENT_M2PERP:
      up->calc_func = gk_fluid_moments_m2perp;
      break;
    case GKYL_F_MOMENT_M3PAR:
      up->calc_func = gk_fluid_moments_m3par;
      break;
    case GKYL_F_MOMENT_M3PERP:
      up->calc_func = gk_fluid_moments_m3perp;
      break;
    case GKYL_F_MOMENT_MAXWELLIAN:
      up->num_mom = 3;
      up->calc_func = gk_fluid_moments_maxwellian;
      break;
    case GKYL_F_MOMENT_BIMAXWELLIAN:
      up->num_mom = 4;
      up->calc_func = gk_fluid_moments_bimaxwellian;
      break;
    case GKYL_F_MOMENT_M0M1M2:
      up->num_mom = 3;
      up->calc_func = gk_fluid_moments_m0m1m2;
      break;
    case GKYL_F_MOMENT_M0M1M2PARM2PERP:
      up->num_mom = 4;
      up->calc_func = gk_fluid_moments_m0m1m2parperp;
      break;
    case GKYL_F_MOMENT_HAMILTONIAN:
      up->num_mom = 3;
      up->calc_func = gk_fluid_moments_hamiltonian;
      break;
    default:
      gkyl_exit("Unsupported gyrokinetic fluid moment.");
  }

  for (int d = 0; d < inp->grid->ndim; ++d) {
    up->volnorm_fac *= inp->grid->dx[d] / sqrt(2.0);
  }

  int nb = inp->basis->num_basis;

  up->bmag = gkyl_array_acquire(inp->bmag);
  up->upar = mkarr(inp->use_gpu, nb, inp->range_ext->volume);
  up->ppar = mkarr(inp->use_gpu, nb, inp->range_ext->volume);
  up->pperp = mkarr(inp->use_gpu, nb, inp->range_ext->volume);
  up->result = mkarr(inp->use_gpu, 4 * nb, inp->range_ext->volume);
  up->mem = inp->use_gpu ? gkyl_dg_bin_op_mem_cu_dev_new(inp->range->volume, nb) :
                           gkyl_dg_bin_op_mem_new(inp->range->volume, nb);

#ifdef GKYL_HAVE_CUDA
  if (inp->use_gpu && inp->integrated) {
    up->final_func = gkyl_gk_fluid_moments_integrate_cu;
  }
#endif

  return up;
}

int
gkyl_gk_fluid_moments_num_mom(const struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *up)
{
  return up->num_mom;
}

void
gkyl_gk_fluid_moments_advance(
  const struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *up, const struct gkyl_range *range,
  const struct gkyl_array *state, const struct gkyl_array *phi, struct gkyl_array *out
)
{
  assert(range->volume == up->num_cells);
  up->calc_func(up, range, state, phi);
  up->final_func(up, range, out);
}

void
gkyl_gk_fluid_moments_from_prim(
  const struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *up, const struct gkyl_range *range,
  const struct gkyl_array *prim, const struct gkyl_array *jacobgeo, struct gkyl_array *state
)
{
  int nb = up->basis.num_basis;
  assert(range->volume == up->num_cells);
  // Weight density first so recovery inverts the same weak products.
  gkyl_dg_mul_op_range(&up->basis, 0, up->upar, 0, jacobgeo, 0, prim, range);
  gkyl_array_set_offset_ncoeff_range(state, up->mass, up->upar, nb, 0, 0, range);
  gkyl_dg_mul_op_range(&up->basis, 1, state, 0, state, 1, prim, range);
  gkyl_dg_mul_op_range(&up->basis, 0, up->ppar, 0, state, 2, prim, range);
  gk_fluid_moments_calc_Jpperp_from_prim(up, range, state, prim);
  gkyl_dg_mul_op_range(&up->basis, 0, up->upar, 1, prim, 1, state, range);
  gkyl_array_accumulate_range(up->upar, 1.0, up->ppar, range);
  gkyl_array_scale_range(up->upar, 0.5, range);
  gkyl_array_accumulate_range(up->upar, 1.0, up->pperp, range);
  gkyl_array_set_offset_ncoeff_range(state, 1.0, up->upar, nb, 0, 2 * nb, range);
  gkyl_dg_div_op_range(up->mem, &up->basis, 3, state, 0, up->pperp, 0, up->bmag, range);
}

void
gkyl_gk_fluid_moments_set_density(
  const struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *up, const struct gkyl_range *range,
  const struct gkyl_array *density, struct gkyl_array *state
)
{
  int nb = up->basis.num_basis;
  assert(range->volume == up->num_cells);
  gkyl_array_set_offset_range(up->ppar, up->mass, density, 0, range);
  gkyl_dg_div_op_range(up->mem, &up->basis, 0, up->upar, 0, up->ppar, 0, state, range);
  for (int c = 1; c < 4; ++c) {
    gkyl_dg_mul_op_range(&up->basis, c, state, 0, up->upar, c, state, range);
  }
  gkyl_array_set_offset_ncoeff_range(state, 1.0, up->ppar, nb, 0, 0, range);
}

void
gkyl_gk_fluid_moments_release(struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *up)
{
  gkyl_array_release(up->bmag);
  gkyl_array_release(up->upar);
  gkyl_array_release(up->ppar);
  gkyl_array_release(up->pperp);
  gkyl_array_release(up->result);
  gkyl_dg_bin_op_mem_release(up->mem);
  gkyl_free(up);
}
extern "C" {
#include <gkyl_gk_fluid_moments_priv.h>
}

__global__ static void
gk_fluid_moments_integrate_kernel(
  int nb, int nm, double rmass_fac, struct gkyl_range range, const struct gkyl_array *result,
  struct gkyl_array *out
)
{
  int idx[GKYL_MAX_DIM];
  for (long cell = threadIdx.x + blockIdx.x * blockDim.x; cell < range.volume;
       cell += gridDim.x * blockDim.x) {
    gkyl_sub_range_inv_idx(&range, cell, idx);
    long loc = gkyl_range_idx(&range, idx);
    const double *dg = (const double *)gkyl_array_cfetch(result, loc);
    double *integral = (double *)gkyl_array_fetch(out, loc);
    for (int c = 0; c < nm; ++c) {
      integral[c] = rmass_fac * dg[c * nb];
    }
  }
}

void
gkyl_gk_fluid_moments_integrate_cu(
  const struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *up, const struct gkyl_range *range, struct gkyl_array *out
)
{
  gk_fluid_moments_integrate_kernel<<<range->nblocks, range->nthreads>>>(
    up->basis.num_basis, up->num_mom, up->volnorm_fac, *range, up->result->on_dev, out->on_dev
  );
}
#pragma once

#include <gkyl_gk_fluid_moments.h>
#include <gkyl_dg_bin_ops.h>

struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments {
  struct gkyl_basis basis; // Configuration-space basis.
  int num_mom; // Number of output moments.
  int component; // Conservative-state component used for M0, M1, or M2.
  long num_cells; // Batch size of the weak division solves.
  double mass, charge; // Species mass and charge.
  double volnorm_fac; // Converts the constant DG coefficient to a cell integral.
  double rmass_fac; // State-to-moment factor: 1/m for M0 and M1, 2/m for M2.
  struct gkyl_array *bmag; // Acquired magnetic-field magnitude.
  struct gkyl_array *upar; // Parallel-velocity buffer, also reused for conversion and scaling.
  struct gkyl_array *ppar; // Jacobian-weighted parallel-pressure buffer and intermediate results.
  struct gkyl_array *pperp; // Jacobian-weighted perpendicular-pressure buffer.
  struct gkyl_array *result; // DG coefficients of calculated moments, before output or integration.
  gkyl_dg_bin_op_mem *mem; // Preallocated workspace for weak-DG division.
  // Methods selected at initialization:
  // Calculate the requested moments into result.
  void (*calc_func)(const struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *, const struct gkyl_range *, const struct gkyl_array *, const struct gkyl_array *);
  // Copy DG moments to output or compute their cell integrals.
  void (*final_func)(const struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *, const struct gkyl_range *, struct gkyl_array *);
};

#ifdef GKYL_HAVE_CUDA
/** Extract constant coefficients as cell integrals on the GPU.
 * @param up Fluid updater with DG results in its buffer array.
 * @param range Configuration subrange.
 * @param out Output cell integrals.
 */
void gkyl_gk_fluid_moments_integrate_cu(
  const struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments *up, const struct gkyl_range *range, struct gkyl_array *out
);
#endif
  if (!sm->is_integrated) {
    gkyl_dg_bin_op_mem_release(sm->mem_geo);
  }
}

static void
gk_species_moment_init_fluid(
  struct gkyl_gyrokinetic_app *app, struct gk_species *gks, struct gk_species_moment *sm,
  enum gkyl_distribution_moments mom_type
)
{
  sm->gf_moms = gkyl_gk_fluid_moments_inew(&(struct gkyl_gk_fluid_moments_inp){
    .basis = &app->basis,
    .grid = &app->grid,
    .range = &app->local,
    .range_ext = &app->local_ext,
    .bmag = app->gk_geom->geo_int.bmag,
    .mass = gks->info.mass,
    .charge = gks->info.charge,
    .moment = mom_type,
    .integrated = sm->is_integrated,
    .use_gpu = app->use_gpu,
  });
  sm->fluid_phi = app->field->phi_smooth;
  sm->num_mom = gkyl_gk_fluid_moments_num_mom(sm->gf_moms);
  sm->marr = mkarr(
    app->use_gpu, sm->num_mom * (sm->is_integrated ? 1 : app->basis.num_basis),
    app->local_ext.volume
  );
  sm->marr_host = app->use_gpu ? mkarr(false, sm->marr->ncomp, sm->marr->size) : sm->marr;
  if (!sm->is_integrated) {
    sm->mem_geo = app->use_gpu ?
                    gkyl_dg_bin_op_mem_cu_dev_new(app->local.volume, app->basis.num_basis) :
                    gkyl_dg_bin_op_mem_new(app->local.volume, app->basis.num_basis);
    sm->diag_jacobgeo_div_func = sm->is_maxwellian_moms || sm->is_bimaxwellian_moms ?
                                   gk_species_moment_diag_jacobgeo_div_enabled_1st_comp :
                                   gk_species_moment_diag_jacobgeo_div_enabled_all_comp;
  }
  sm->calc_func = gk_species_moment_calc_fluid;
  sm->release_func = gk_species_moment_release_fluid;
}

void
gk_species_moment_init(
  struct gkyl_gyrokinetic_app *app, struct gk_species *gks, struct gk_species_moment *sm,
  enum gkyl_distribution_moments mom_type, bool is_integrated
)
{
  sm->is_integrated = is_integrated;
  sm->is_maxwellian_moms = mom_type == GKYL_F_MOMENT_MAXWELLIAN;
  sm->is_bimaxwellian_moms = mom_type == GKYL_F_MOMENT_BIMAXWELLIAN;
  sm->diag_jacobgeo_div_func = gk_species_moment_diag_jacobgeo_div_disabled;

  if (gks->is_fluid) {
