# Dispatch CUDA integration inside the integration function

## Changes

Keep `result` and the public API unchanged.

At the beginning of `gk_fluid_moments_integrate`, add:

```c
#ifdef GKYL_HAVE_CUDA
  assert(gkyl_array_is_cu_dev(out) == gkyl_array_is_cu_dev(up->result));
  if (gkyl_array_is_cu_dev(out)) {
    gkyl_gk_fluid_moments_integrate_cu(up, range, out);
    return;
  }
#endif
```

Remove the constructor’s CUDA-specific reassignment of `up->final_func`. Its existing initializer will continue selecting integration or copying. Leave the CPU loop and CUDA implementation unchanged.

## Verification

Format the file and run the fluid-moment tests and focused fluid-species regression. Confirm no failures beyond the known M2 scaling issue. Run CUDA integrated-moment tests when available; otherwise report that limitation.

